3. Agent Deployment Scripts & Prompts
For each agent, add a section in your project’s README, Discord bot configuration or task manager with the following template. Replace placeholder text with your system’s commands or code.

Revenue Agent (Auto‑Payday)
Trigger: Daily at 10:00 GMT and whenever a sale or lead event occurs.

Prompt:

“Scan all sales data and notify of any drops or big wins. Suggest a promotional offer if no sales occur within the past 48 hours.”

Output: A summary in your #team-sync channel, tagging the admin. Award BROski$ to the top seller.

Onboarding Agent (Conversion Booster)
Trigger: Each time a user joins Discord or subscribes via email.

Prompt:

“Send a dopamine‑charged welcome message along with a unique offer. Track and report conversion metrics.”

Output: A DM log, XP assignment and an update to the new user’s streak status.

Streak & Celebration Agent (Motivation Engine)
Trigger: Whenever a user achieves a streak (e.g., three consecutive days of activity) or a sales milestone is reached.

Prompt:

“Automatically celebrate with a custom GIF, sound, tag, and bonus BROski$.”

Output: A public hype message in Discord, plus updates to the streak leaderboard.

Content Suggestion Agent (Money‑Maker)
Trigger: Weekly, or after each top‑performing post.

Prompt:

“Analyze the last week’s top‑performing content and products. Suggest three new money‑making posts or products for next week.”

Output: A list of actions sent to the #content-team, with tasks assigned to the appropriate team members.

Security Agent (Immortal Guardian)
Trigger: Continuous; run a health check every minute.

Prompt:

“Scan the portal for downtime or suspicious logins. Automatically restart services if needed, log the incident and reward the first responder.”

Output: An uptime log and a bonus streak for the first person who responds to an alert.

Feedback Agent (Continuous Upgrade)
Trigger: Every Friday at 15:00 GMT.

Prompt:

“Collect and synthesize all feedback from team members, users and customers. Identify the top three improvements for next week.”

Output: An innovation queue and XP rewards for contributors.

Outreach Agent (Lead Converter)
Trigger: On low sales days or as part of a scheduled campaign.

Prompt:

“DM or email hot leads with a playful challenge and a unique discount code.”

Output: A conversion report and BROski$ bonuses for the agent or team member responsible.

4. Integration with Discord and Portals
Bot Commands. Provide simple commands to trigger agents manually via Discord, for example:

!agent-revenue scan

!agent-onboard new

!agent-streak celebrate

!agent-content suggest

!agent-feedback run

!agent-security scan

Reward Automation. Automatically assign BROski$ whenever an agent completes a task successfully. Keep track of XP, streaks and badges.

Celebration Posts. Configure your bot to post GIFs, emojis or short videos in #team-sync whenever a milestone is reached. Use tags to highlight the top performer or agent.

Leaderboards. Update weekly leaderboards for top earners, streak holders and innovators. Display them in Discord or on your portal dashboard.

5. Revenue Loop & Feedback Cycle
Scan revenue. The Revenue Agent reviews all sales and highlights dips or opportunities.

Trigger outreach or promotions. When the system detects a lull, the Outreach Agent sends special offers to leads or posts flash sales.

Monitor conversions & celebrate. Streak & Celebration Agents cheer on successes, awarding BROski$ for significant wins.

Collect feedback. The Feedback Agent gathers insights and suggests improvements for offers, products and processes.

Iterate. The Content Agent and Revenue Agent incorporate feedback into new campaigns and product ideas, closing the loop.

Repeat this cycle daily or weekly to ensure continuous improvement and momentum.

6. Weekly Ritual
Friday: Agents drop reports in #team-sync or on the portal dashboard. Celebrate the top agent, top human and top win with instant BROski$ and a Discord party (GIF, badge, tag).

Saturday: Hold a quick sync meeting to review feedback and assign next week’s upgrades.

Sunday: Rest and reset.

Monday: Launch the new theme or mission and restart the loop.

7. Final Notes
Keep your environment variables secure. Do not commit API keys to version control; store them in Vercel’s environment settings or a secure secrets manager
